#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "70991204-370a-5804-a04e-7e664db052de" :question/math-academy-id "e-8048" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- $R_1 := \\ldots$\n\n- $R_3:=R_3-3R_2$\n\n- $R_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_2,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below $a_{22}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_1 := R_1 - 2R_2\\quad$ and $\\quad R_4:=R_4+2R_2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161690 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf8e85c-ffa6-55b9-a087-2a5272f10f25" :question/math-academy-id "e-8049" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- $C_1:=\\ldots$\n\n- $C_3:= C_3 - 4C_2$\n\n- $C_4:= \\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_2,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{32}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & -1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 11 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -23 & -3 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+5C_2\\quad$ and $\\quad C_4:=C_4-2C_2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "399b7598-c793-5032-9f33-ac02c7b85fe1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8050" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_1,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below $a_{11}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_2:=R_2-2R_1\\quad$ and $\\quad R_3:=R_3+3R_1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f9912357-1d1d-5413-917e-257dc5dfc0fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-8051" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_3,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+6{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+5{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & -17 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $C_1:=C_1+6C_3\\quad$ and $\\quad C_2:=C_2+5C_3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c44493f8-23ea-5a6c-bfae-1a92fb860e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305749} {:answer/id #uuid "f2aafdfc-934a-5bca-82f4-ffee306f0997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305750} {:answer/id #uuid "df86e49d-66c6-5c6e-b3c3-18a526bd9ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305751} {:answer/id #uuid "76d8a9d5-46c7-52cd-91e5-47f5598584bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305752} {:answer/id #uuid "55fe4381-f7da-5ef5-a6f1-95b2768c8ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c44493f8-23ea-5a6c-bfae-1a92fb860e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305749} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0421097-be3b-5147-9673-531d1d817fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eecdf20-11a2-5ff3-9b1e-3ac77ced4618" :question/math-academy-id "q-130444" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{32}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff61e5cc-d9b3-5cdc-9b06-16d814bc9c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-5{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305756} {:answer/id #uuid "03a75da7-5f3d-532d-ac8c-e887f63944f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305757} {:answer/id #uuid "076048fe-dea3-5ccc-9d70-6ce6f502f00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305758} {:answer/id #uuid "36bc2733-e05a-5043-9b68-59ec309fa576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305759} {:answer/id #uuid "c6436872-251b-59d3-ac84-bce5e5242108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076048fe-dea3-5ccc-9d70-6ce6f502f00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305758} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6681889-8bf2-51ba-b2ca-fb60a90d4d95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9109ca13-9f72-5fb4-b7bd-9f317ed19eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130610" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 15 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+5{C}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0880b08-b2df-5d46-81f3-6856180cf816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305763} {:answer/id #uuid "8f97737b-3d74-5cdd-8673-bce5602d0946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-4{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305764} {:answer/id #uuid "90a236fd-a777-54fa-88c5-dcd4e52aa3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305765} {:answer/id #uuid "7738f6b5-7231-5059-bd97-75004833c7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-4{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305766} {:answer/id #uuid "46a09f28-a0ab-51db-9cb4-b41406924ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46a09f28-