{3}:=…$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{23}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 0 & -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941c4e1-5e36-53ce-bc6b-7d6663d0963c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} + 4C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} - 3C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160525} {:answer/id #uuid "f458abd4-da18-5702-90a4-330e62adc6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1} - 3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2} + C_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160526} {:answer/id #uuid "1dabc275-1f78-58e5-af0a-2f8732ba71e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value