ed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{13}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf23d96-28ea-5671-bdca-4e0c9c4782ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305798} {:answer/id #uuid "41db955a-a882-5147-8cde-3f306ac4cfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305799} {:answer/id #uuid "c15d5562-76b0-5349-a76b-7d58f8ab8c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305800} {:answer/id #uuid "76573182-471d-5f16-aecb-252537e87bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305801} {:answer/id #uuid "95bd875b-033b-5258-a8bd-9b820d91ac55" :answer/type {: