med into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{23}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79fa33b-b535-5339-87f4-c6b4865abc9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-5{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305805} {:answer/id #uuid "8979b792-55e4-54c9-bfc5-98b9aaaa9d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305806} {:answer/id #uuid "895876d5-9a62-5b9e-b79a-8747e73ec064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305807} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec9085b-52d9-5ee4-80da-a96c3997f150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305808} {:answer/id #uuid "eb98513a-3da1-532e-8135-ec925695d