],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of ${a}_{13}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -7 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73e44e06-5553-5910-91b8-a7e0477291e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305833} {:answer/id #uuid "699c0ded-059f-5abb-b7b9-51c0ccaca33c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305834} {:answer/id #uuid "76cd1e2f-f84b-5047-bdda-16d49c47487e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305835} {:answer/id #uuid "01097d7c-5dac-5aaf-ab3b-8f48c42eba44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305836} {:answer/id #uuid "6712840e-9eaf-56e9-a578-f1780e809c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76cd1e2f-f84b-5047-bdda-16d49c47487e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305835} :answer-field/id #uuid "85233076-8b84-55c3-a82b-6e5a34e85311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eead9a93-3bb6-58a4-aeab-6e0aad8565b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-91210" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 7 \\\\ -7 & -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 4 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -19 & 5 & -14 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- ${C}_{1}:=…$\n- ${C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{2}$\n- ${C}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 4 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -19 & 5 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 4 & -5 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -19 & 5 & -14 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 4 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -19 & 5 & -14 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b59188b1-8521-56fd-84dc-06aa973c8a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305840} {:answer/id #uuid "f2856fba-8f06-59db-bb3d-842289a9fac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305841} {:answer/id #uuid "71c37254-8d77-5011-84c8-83e3d528d77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305842} {:answer/id #uuid "15f056b8-189c-5730-9db4-0bb93d78cf56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305843} {:answer/id #uuid "eb237e1d-e478-5c35-b3f9-7097b77f65c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-7{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15f056b8-